Kristoffer Björkman <kristoffer.bjorkman@frontnet.org> wrote:
[turning undead]
> I'm not sure about how the chance to resist works, probably based on 
> your and monster's levels. Somone else might answer this better.

The monster resists if a random number >= 0 and less than 
  100 + your level - the monster's level
is less than the monster's magic resistance.  This latter number is 30 
for liches, 60 for demiliches, and 90 for master and arch-liches; 50 for 
ghosts and 0 for shades; 25 for vampires and 50 for vampire lords; 5 for 
barrow wights; 15 for wraiths, and 25 for Nazgul; 20 or 30 for mummies; 
and 0 for zombies, ghouls, and skeletons.  

As Kristoffer mentioned, the same calculation is performed again to see 
if the monster is (not only scared but) destroyed.

The problem with turning undead is that it paralyzes you for five turns.
A monster could even start fleeing, come back, and beat up on you before 
you snap out of it.  This usually makes it useless.  Perhaps combined 
with Elbereth...

